":"Ingredient in 4 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Olive oil is a vegetable oil obtained by pressing whole olives (the fruit of Olea europaea, a traditional tree crop of the Mediterranean Basin) and extracting the oil."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-extra-virgin-olive-oil"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extra_virgin_olive_oil"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Rafanata","dish/rafanata"],["Spaghetti alla Nerano","dish/spaghetti-alla-nerano"]]],["Palestinian cuisine","cuisine/palestinian-cuisine",[["Maltout","dish/maltout"]]],["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine",[["Parmigiana","dish/parmigiana"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Olive oil","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":3005644,"top":[["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",1092358],["Italy","cuisine/italian-cuisine",340022],["Greece","cuisine/greek-cuisine",252381],["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",248429],["Tunisia","cuisine/tunisian-cuisine",247325],["Morocco","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",165300],["Portugal","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",162309],["Syria","cuisine/syrian-cuisine",130197],["Algeria","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",88525],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",41450],["Argentina","cuisine/argentine-cuisine",31000],["Jordan","cuisine/jordanian-cuisine",24563],["Palestine","cuisine/palestinian-cuisine",22628],["Chile","cuisine/chilean-cuisine",22550],["Albania","cuisine/cuisine-of-albania",21750]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Basil","ingredient/basil"],["Parmesan","ingredient/parmesan"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Mozzarella","ingredient/mozzarella"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Horseradish","ingredient/horseradish"],["Pecorino","ingredient/pecorino"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Provolone","ingredient/provolone"],["Spaghetti","ingredient/spaghetti"],["Zucchini","ingredient/zucchini"]]}]},"ingredient/ladyfinger-biscuit":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/ladyfinger-biscuit","n":"Ladyfinger (biscuit)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Ladyfingers or Naples biscuits, in British English sponge fingers, also known by the Italian name savoiardi or by the French name boudoirs (French: [budwaʁ]), are low-density, dry, egg-based, sweet sponge cake biscuits roughly shaped like large fingers. They are a principal ingredient in many dessert recipes, such as trifles and charlottes, and are also used as fruit or chocolate gateau linings, and for the sponge element of tiramisu. They are typically soaked in a sugar syrup or liqueur, or in espresso for tiramisu."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-ladyfinger-biscuit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladyfinger_(biscuit)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Tiramisu","dish/tiramisu"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Savoiarde PAT","ingredient/savoiarde-pat"],["Carabao mango","ingredient/carabao-mango"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Cracker","ingredient/cracker"],["Graham crackers","ingredient/graham-crackers"],["Mango","ingredient/mango"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"],["Cocoa powder","ingredient/cocoa-powder"],["Coffee","ingredient/coffee"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Espresso","ingr